!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/meta-picks.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/38/m/meta-kernel.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/38/m/meta.tn"
@doc:"""
  A meta layer holding one slot of each by-name spelling, so a schema it governs is where both are judged. `orders`
  maps identifiers to `order` records; `rpick.m` is typed `ref<order>`, naming a value of `order`, which a governed
  schema holds only as a key of an entry built with `orders` (`os.o1`); `pick.t` is typed `kind<record>`, naming a
  record type of the governed schema's own closure. `order` itself is this layer's record, and no name of a governed
  schema resolves to it. An entry built with a namespace type is a value, not a type, and a processor that binds
  binds each value of its map to a host class of its own: the records `order`, `rpick` and `pick`.
  """
{
  order  => { id: text }
  orders => namespace & { key_type: = identifier  value_type: = order }
  rpick  => { m: ref<order> }
  rpicks => namespace & { key_type: = identifier  value_type: = rpick }
  pick   => { t: kind<record> }
  picks  => namespace & { key_type: = identifier  value_type: = pick }
}
